# Held container updates for scripts that move many items (server/README.md "Auto Seller: one update per sale"). Each
# item a script removes from, adds to or moves inside an open container sent its own packet (remove / add / update
# container item) and, for a carried container, a full stats packet (Player::postRemoveNotification -> sendStats). The
# client then redraws the whole container window two or three times per packet (onSizeChange, onRemoveItem): a Loot Bag
# sale of 255 items was 510 packets and about 1500 window refreshes in one frame, the stutter players saw.
# Lua player:beginContainerBatch() / player:endContainerBatch() (nested pairs count) hold those packets: while held,
# Player::sendAdd/Update/RemoveContainerItem only mark the open window ids of the container and sendStats only marks
# the stats; the last end sends one full container packet per marked window that is still open (its page moved back
# when the items it showed are gone) and one stats packet. A batch left open (a script error between the two calls)
# ends by itself at the next update after 2 s. Chaos.containerBatch (chaos_constants.lua) calls the pair with pcall.
# Apply after 0001-0053: patch -p1 < 0054-container-update-batch.patch (in the server folder, next to src/).
--- a/src/luascript.cpp
+++ b/src/luascript.cpp
